CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ trailing-return decltype resolves: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG must FAIL: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
A variadic function template whose trailing-return decltype contains a
forwarding-reference pack expansion (static_cast<Args&&>(a)..., the declaration
of variadic std::__invoke) does not expand the pack in the return type for a
two-or-more-element pack, so the return type fails to resolve and a
decltype(invk(...)) type silently fails (vacuous proof).  Flip to CORE once
trailing-return decltype forwarding-reference pack expansion is implemented.
This is the next layer for multi-argument std::function (make_bvrep).
